  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_CH11_DIAGRAM_Q01 - Agarose gel electrophoresis DNA band migration</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>Observe the diagram of a typical agarose gel electrophoresis setup showing DNA bands in lanes 1 to 4. Which statement correctly identifies band <strong>Y</strong> and the direction of DNA migration?</p>
      <p>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 460 200" width="460" height="200">
          <rect x="10" y="10" width="440" height="180" rx="8" fill="#f8fafc" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <rect x="60" y="35" width="340" height="130" fill="#e2e8f0" stroke="#475569" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="35" y="105" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e293b" text-anchor="middle">(-)</text>
          <text x="425" y="105" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#1e293b" text-anchor="middle">(+)</text>
          <text x="85" y="25" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="#334155" text-anchor="middle">Wells</text>
          <rect x="75" y="45" width="16" height="18" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <rect x="75" y="75" width="16" height="18" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <rect x="75" y="105" width="16" height="18" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <rect x="75" y="135" width="16" height="18" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#334155" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <text x="65" y="58" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#334155" text-anchor="end">4</text>
          <text x="65" y="88" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#334155" text-anchor="end">3</text>
          <text x="65" y="118" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#334155" text-anchor="end">2</text>
          <text x="65" y="148" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#334155" text-anchor="end">1</text>
          <rect x="120" y="135" width="12" height="18" fill="#dc2626"/>
          <rect x="145" y="105" width="10" height="18" fill="#dc2626"/>
          <rect x="195" y="105" width="8" height="18" fill="#dc2626"/>
          <rect x="165" y="75" width="10" height="18" fill="#dc2626"/>
          <rect x="210" y="75" width="8" height="18" fill="#dc2626"/>
          <rect x="290" y="75" width="6" height="18" fill="#dc2626"/>
          <rect x="155" y="45" width="10" height="18" fill="#dc2626"/>
          <rect x="225" y="45" width="8" height="18" fill="#dc2626"/>
          <rect x="305" y="45" width="6" height="18" fill="#dc2626"/>
          <rect x="355" y="45" width="5" height="18" fill="#dc2626"/>
          <text x="126" y="178" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f172a" text-anchor="middle">Band X</text>
          <text x="357" y="25" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f172a" text-anchor="middle">Band Y</text>
          <line x1="126" y1="166" x2="126" y2="155" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <line x1="357" y1="28" x2="357" y2="43" stroke="#0f172a" stroke-width="1.2"/>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Diagram Layout</strong><br/>The schematic shows an agarose gel slab with sample wells located near the negative electrode (cathode) on the left and the positive electrode (anode) on the right. Band X is closest to the loading well, whereas band Y has migrated farthest toward the right end.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Governing Principle</strong><br/>DNA fragments carry a net negative charge due to their sugar-phosphate backbone and are separated by size through the sieving effect of the agarose matrix under an electric field.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>Because DNA is negatively charged, it moves away from the cathode and toward the positively charged anode. Smaller DNA fragments pass more easily through the pores of the agarose gel and therefore travel farther from the wells than larger fragments.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Final Conclusion</strong><br/>Band Y, which is farthest from the well, represents the smallest DNA fragments, and the DNA fragments migrate toward the anode.</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Band Y represents the largest DNA fragments, and DNA migrates toward the cathode.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Band Y represents the smallest DNA fragments, and DNA migrates toward the anode.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Band X represents the smallest DNA fragments, and DNA migrates toward the cathode.</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Band Y represents the largest DNA fragments, and DNA migrates toward the anode.</p>]]></text></answer>
