  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_CH11_DIAGRAM_Q03 - Insertional inactivation in cloning vector pBR322</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>Refer to the schematic map of the <em>E. coli</em> cloning vector pBR322 shown below. If a foreign DNA fragment is ligated at the <strong><em>Pst</em> I</strong> restriction site, what will be the antibiotic resistance phenotype of the recombinant <em>E. coli</em> transformants?</p>
      <p>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 360 280" width="360" height="280">
          <rect x="10" y="10" width="340" height="260" rx="8" fill="#f8fafc" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <circle cx="180" cy="140" r="80" fill="none" stroke="#38bdf8" stroke-width="16"/>
          <path d="M 103 118 A 80 80 0 0 1 150 66" fill="none" stroke="#f472b6" stroke-width="16"/>
          <path d="M 210 66 A 80 80 0 0 1 257 162" fill="none" stroke="#f472b6" stroke-width="16"/>
          <path d="M 115 186 A 80 80 0 0 1 142 210" fill="none" stroke="#14b8a6" stroke-width="16"/>
          <path d="M 172 220 A 80 80 0 0 1 198 218" fill="none" stroke="#a3e635" stroke-width="16"/>
          <text x="180" y="145" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="16" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f172a" text-anchor="middle">pBR322</text>
          <text x="135" y="112" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#831843">ampᴿ</text>
          <text x="210" y="112" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="bold" fill="#831843">tetᴿ</text>
          <text x="140" y="188" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f766e">ori</text>
          <text x="185" y="205" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" font-weight="bold" fill="#3f6212">rop</text>
          <line x1="112" y1="88" x2="75" y2="75" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text x="70" y="75" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#1e293b" text-anchor="end">Pst I</text>
          <line x1="126" y1="73" x2="90" y2="52" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text x="85" y="52" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#1e293b" text-anchor="end">Pvu I</text>
          <line x1="172" y1="60" x2="155" y2="35" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text x="155" y="30" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#1e293b" text-anchor="middle">EcoR I</text>
          <line x1="190" y1="60" x2="210" y2="35" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text x="215" y="30" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#1e293b" text-anchor="middle">Hind III</text>
          <line x1="250" y1="100" x2="285" y2="85" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text x="290" y="88" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#1e293b" text-anchor="start">BamH I</text>
          <line x1="258" y1="145" x2="295" y2="145" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text x="300" y="149" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#1e293b" text-anchor="start">Sal I</text>
          <line x1="185" y1="220" x2="185" y2="245" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="1.2"/>
          <text x="185" y="258" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#1e293b" text-anchor="middle">Pvu II</text>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Diagram Layout</strong><br/>The circular plasmid map of pBR322 displays two selectable marker genes: the ampicillin resistance gene (\(\text{amp}^{\text{R}}\)), which contains the <em>Pst</em> I and <em>Pvu</em> I restriction sites, and the tetracycline resistance gene (\(\text{tet}^{\text{R}}\)), which contains the <em>Bam</em>H I and <em>Sal</em> I sites.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Governing Principle</strong><br/>Inserting a foreign DNA fragment within the coding region of an antibiotic resistance gene causes insertional inactivation of that specific gene, while leaving the other antibiotic resistance gene intact and functional.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>Because the <em>Pst</em> I site is located inside the ampicillin resistance gene, ligating foreign DNA at <em>Pst</em> I disrupts \(\text{amp}^{\text{R}}\) and renders the recombinant plasmid sensitive to ampicillin. The tetracycline resistance gene (\(\text{tet}^{\text{R}}\)) remains uninterrupted and continues to confer resistance to tetracycline.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Final Conclusion</strong><br/>The recombinant <em>E. coli</em> transformants will be sensitive to ampicillin but resistant to tetracycline.</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Resistant to both ampicillin and tetracycline</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Sensitive to both ampicillin and tetracycline</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Resistant to ampicillin but sensitive to tetracycline</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>Sensitive to ampicillin but resistant to tetracycline</p>]]></text></answer>
