  <question type="multichoice">
    <name><text>NEET_UG_BIOLOGY_CH11_DIAGRAM_Q04 - Polymerase chain reaction cycle steps</text></name>
    <questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p>The schematic below represents one cycle of Polymerase Chain Reaction (PCR) with three sequential stages labeled <strong>P</strong>, <strong>Q</strong>, and <strong>R</strong>. Identify <strong>P</strong>, <strong>Q</strong>, and <strong>R</strong> in the correct order.</p>
      <p>
        <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 460 270" width="460" height="270">
          <rect x="10" y="10" width="440" height="250" rx="8" fill="#f8fafc" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="1.5"/>
          <line x1="60" y1="40" x2="320" y2="40" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="2"/>
          <line x1="60" y1="54" x2="320" y2="54" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="2"/>
          <rect x="120" y="40" width="140" height="14" fill="#ef4444" opacity="0.7"/>
          <text x="45" y="44" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#1e293b">5'</text>
          <text x="328" y="44" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#1e293b">3'</text>
          <text x="45" y="58" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#1e293b">3'</text>
          <text x="328" y="58" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#1e293b">5'</text>
          <line x1="190" y1="62" x2="190" y2="85" stroke="#65a30d" stroke-width="2.5"/>
          <polygon points="190,88 185,80 195,80" fill="#65a30d"/>
          <text x="205" y="78" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#334155">Heat</text>
          <text x="370" y="78" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f172a">Step P</text>
          <line x1="60" y1="100" x2="320" y2="100" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="2"/>
          <rect x="220" y="104" width="40" height="8" fill="#ef4444"/>
          <line x1="60" y1="132" x2="320" y2="132" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="2"/>
          <rect x="120" y="120" width="40" height="8" fill="#ef4444"/>
          <text x="370" y="120" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f172a">Step Q</text>
          <text x="275" y="114" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#475569">Primers</text>
          <line x1="190" y1="142" x2="190" y2="170" stroke="#65a30d" stroke-width="2.5"/>
          <polygon points="190,173 185,165 195,165" fill="#65a30d"/>
          <text x="205" y="160" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="11" fill="#334155">Taq polymerase + dNTPs</text>
          <line x1="60" y1="192" x2="320" y2="192" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="2"/>
          <rect x="120" y="192" width="140" height="12" fill="#ef4444" opacity="0.7"/>
          <line x1="120" y1="204" x2="260" y2="204" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="2"/>
          <line x1="60" y1="226" x2="320" y2="226" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="2"/>
          <rect x="120" y="214" width="140" height="12" fill="#ef4444" opacity="0.7"/>
          <line x1="120" y1="214" x2="260" y2="214" stroke="#1e293b" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="370" y="212" font-family="Arial, sans-serif" font-size="13" font-weight="bold" fill="#0f172a">Step R</text>
        </svg>
      </p>
    ]]></text></questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[
      <p><strong>Step 1: Diagram Layout</strong><br/>The schematic depicts three consecutive stages of a PCR thermal cycle: stage P shows heat separating the double-stranded DNA template, stage Q shows short complementary primers binding to the single-stranded templates, and stage R shows <em>Taq</em> polymerase synthesising new complementary strands using deoxynucleotides.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 2: Governing Principle</strong><br/>In vitro DNA amplification by PCR relies on repeated cycles of thermal strand separation, primer hybridisation, and enzymatic DNA synthesis.</p>
      <p><strong>Step 3: Step-by-Step Working</strong><br/>First, high temperature breaks hydrogen bonds to separate the double-stranded DNA into single strands, which is denaturation (P). Next, the temperature is lowered so that synthetic oligonucleotide primers base-pair to their complementary target regions, which is primer annealing (Q). Finally, thermostable <em>Taq</em> polymerase extends the primers using nucleotides to synthesise new DNA strands, which is extension (R).</p>
      <p><strong>Step 4: Final Conclusion</strong><br/>The correct sequence is P: Denaturation, Q: Annealing, and R: Extension.</p>
    ]]></text></generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>4.0000000</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.2500000</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <single>true</single>
    <shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers>
    <answernumbering>abc</answernumbering>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P: Annealing, Q: Denaturation, R: Extension</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P: Extension, Q: Annealing, R: Denaturation</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="100" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P: Denaturation, Q: Annealing, R: Extension</p>]]></text></answer>
    <answer fraction="0" format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p>P: Denaturation, Q: Extension, R: Annealing</p>]]></text></answer>
